      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The electoral college is undemocratic because it gives disproportionate weight to swing states and rural areas, allowing candidates to focus on a select few voters rather than the entire country. Proponents argue that this system leads to a candidate winning the presidency without receiving the most popular votes, as seen in the 2000 and 2016 presidential elections. Additionally, the electoral college's winner-takes-all approach can result in a candidate winning a state without receiving a majority of the votes within that state, further eroding the democratic process.",
      "source": "target",
